    "industrial_process_notes": "Eduard Simon first isolated the material from storax resin in 1839, naming it 'Styroloxyd'. IG Farben began industrial manufacture in Ludwigshafen around 1931 with pellet extrusion technology; Dow Chemical later commercialized foam variants, patenting Styrofoam in 1944. Free-radical polymerization of styrene yields chains of several thousand monomer units (MW 100,000-400,000 g/mol).",
